    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177">

                <pb facs="0295" n="221" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg221"/>

                <head>Sir F. Bruce to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 7, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Sri Henry Parkes having reported to her
                    Majesty’s government the proceedings which he had adopted last November, in
                    concert with the representatives of the other treaty powers, in order to secure
                    the settlement of the questions now at issue in Japan, I am instructed by her
                    Majesty’s principal secretary of state for foreign affairs to express to the
                    government of the United States the satisfaction of that of her Majesty at the
                    cordiality with which the representatives <pb facs="0296" n="222" xml:id="pg222"
                    /> of Great Britain and the United States co-operate in a matter of such great
                    importance to the two countries.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FREDERICK W. A. BRUCE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
